narrative:
## From Chaos to Clarity

A single massive `main()` function that prints your entire day is hard to read. The solution? Break it into logical chunks — each chunk becomes its own function.

### Before: One Big Mess

```xiom
fn main() -> Int {
  io.println("6:00 AM - Wake up");
  io.println("6:30 AM - Exercise");
  io.println("7:00 AM - Breakfast");
  io.println("9:00 AM - Code review");
  io.println("12:00 PM - Lunch");
  io.println("1:00 PM - Meetings");
  io.println("5:00 PM - Gym");
  io.println("7:00 PM - Dinner");
  io.println("9:00 PM - Read");
  io.println("10:30 PM - Sleep");
  return 0;
}
```

### After: Clean Sections

```xiom
fn morning_routine() {
  io.println("6:00 AM - Wake up");
  io.println("6:30 AM - Exercise");
  io.println("7:00 AM - Breakfast");
}

fn afternoon_routine() {
  io.println("9:00 AM - Code review");
  io.println("12:00 PM - Lunch");
  io.println("1:00 PM - Meetings");
}

fn evening_routine() {
  io.println("5:00 PM - Gym");
  io.println("7:00 PM - Dinner");
  io.println("9:00 PM - Read");
  io.println("10:30 PM - Sleep");
}

fn main() -> Int {
  io.println("=== My Daily Schedule ===");
  morning_routine();
  afternoon_routine();
  evening_routine();
  io.println("=== End of Day ===");
  return 0;
}
```

Each function has one clear responsibility. If you want to change your morning schedule, you know exactly where to look.

